<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\calC ' = \Sing | \sCoNerve [K^{op}] |$ be the “fibrant replacement” for $\calC =\sCoNerve [K^{op}]$. We endow $\Set _{\Delta }^{\calC '}$ with the <em>projective</em> model structure described in §<a href="/tag/" data-tag="">None</a>. 
    <p>
      We note that the Yoneda embedding factors as a composition 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  K \stackrel{j'}{\rightarrow } \sNerve ( (\Set _{\Delta }^{\calC '})^{\circ } ) \stackrel{j''}{\rightarrow } \Fun ( K^{op}, \SSet ), \]
</div>
    <p>
       where $j''$ is the map of Proposition <a href="/tag/AAC4A7" data-tag="AAC4A7">4.2.4.4</a> and consequently a categorical equivalence. It therefore suffices to prove that $j'$ is fully faithful. For this, we need only show that the adjoint map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  J: \sCoNerve [K] \rightarrow \Set _{\Delta }^{\calC '}. \]
</div>
    <p>
       is a fully-faithful functor between simplicial categories. We now observe that $J$ is the composition of an equivalence $\sCoNerve [K] \rightarrow (\calC ')^{op}$ with the (simplicial enriched) Yoneda embedding $(\calC ')^{op} \rightarrow \Set _{\Delta }^{\calC '}$, which is fully faithful in virtue of the classical (simplicially enriched) version of Yoneda's Lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>